    "findings": [
      "The seven formal pages and connected catalog data consistently cover exactly three actual bindings: lasgun_p1_m1, lasgun_p1_m2, and lasgun_p1_m3, with the corresponding three weapon_trait_bespoke_lasgun_p1_increased_zoom variants. The compatibility page, map, reverse Infantry Lasgun index, and UI evidence agree on the actual marks and names.",
      "The held-slot plus alternate-fire condition, not a hit, activates the .85 target conditional attribute. The trait has no hit stacks, blessing TTL, or independent countdown. Zoomed shooting and the zoomed special remain in ADS; the hipfire special is the flashlight path. Cache and camera updates govern first visible application and exit, so the text makes no same-frame promise.",
      "Tier I-IV all provide .85. The same-key .95 wrapper conditional is fallback and is replaced by the tier stat while its held/alternate-fire gate remains. RAW English and Traditional Chinese strings are reproduced exactly with their hashes; the formatter has no tier placeholder and reconstructs the same fixed RAW string at every tier. The comparison correctly distinguishes the numeric runtime value from qualitative RAW wording without inventing a RAW tier placeholder.",
      "The camera math distinguishes the .85 target attribute from the smoothed r_prev and r_now samples. The 32.5125-degree example is explicitly controlled math under first-person ADS, completed transition, r_prev=r_now=.85, and external/global factors of 1; it is not presented as a measured or guaranteed stable in-game angle. The per-frame update/getter order and degrees-to-radians conversion are consistent with the cited camera and AlternateFire evidence.",
      "The image identifier weapon_trait_045, full game icon path, and attachment URL are separate and consistent with the image receipt and formal/map association."
    ],
